<title>POLAND: Polish grain prices slipped last week.</title>
<headline>Polish grain prices slipped last week.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Agriculture Ministry said in a statement that wheat, barley and rye prices slipped during last week's grain auctions.</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>  Product   week to Feb 15    previous week   yr/yr growth</p>
<p>   Wheat	56.79 zl/q	 57.21 zl/q	  9.2 pct</p>
<p>   Rye	  42.20 zl/q	 42.32 zl/q	 27.9 pct</p>
<p>   Barley     49.37 zl/q	 50.39 zl/q	  7.3 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - zl/q = zlotys per quintal.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
